 ### Unwritten attachment stores without lookahead
 
-- **Symptom:** read-only depth/stencil attachments are written back after every pass, and the periodic unwritten-store savings counter remains zero with the default configuration.
-- **Cause:** `udc_note_draw` and `sd_finish` returned early when `DM_NVN_TBDR` was off. This also disabled the local unwritten-attachment proof, although it does not depend on future sampled-texture readers. The broader lookahead remains disabled because it does not understand bindless readers.
-- **Fix:** collect per-pass write facts independently of the lookahead switch and omit only stores of attachments that were loaded and provably unchanged. Clears, depth writes, stencil writes and possible writable image/atomic/storage aliases retain their stores. Lookahead, pass merging and cross-submission invalidation remain disabled. `DM_NVN_UNWRITTEN_DC=0` restores store-all behavior.
-- **Check:** `make -C dm/gfx/tests GAME=<id> check_t_unwritten_store` performs real GPU readback against a store-all control and literal color/depth/stencil values, with lookahead disabled. It covers read-only depth/stencil, depth writes, stencil writes, pending clears, and writable images (including native image atomics) and both storage-buffer binding forms. `t_unwritten_store --bench` runs a synthetic 32-pass 1080p workload with balanced on/off order; it is not a game FPS measurement.
-- **Found on:** [NieR:Automata US 1.0.3](../../dm/games/010056B015FE8000/README.md#factory-combat-capture-and-9s-texture-follow-up), during iPhone factory-combat performance investigation. The change passes the GPU proof and rendering regressions on Mac; iPhone gameplay benefit remains to be measured.
+- **Symptom:** a later pass can read undefined color/depth/stencil contents after a loaded but unchanged attachment was discarded. Source follow-up to periodic bright-light flashes in Odyssey identified this contract violation; the specific visible flash cause is not yet confirmed on device.
+- **Cause:** the former local proof assumed that a loaded attachment not written in this pass still had valid backing after a DontCare store. Metal explicitly allows DontCare to replace attachment contents with arbitrary data, even if earlier device readbacks happened to preserve them. Absence of writes does not prove absence of later readers.
+- **Fix:** `sd_finish` retains Store unless an independent lifetime decision marks the contents dead. Write tracking and its diagnostic override remain, but cannot by themselves discard an attachment. The broader optional lookahead/cross-submission policy is unchanged and remains off in the default Odyssey configuration. No bloom clamp, shader change or timing delay is used.
+- **Check:** `run_attachment_store_native.py` executes the production store decision with a conforming encoder model that poisons discarded data, checking later reads of color, depth and stencil. The former decision is a failing negative control; independently dead attachments may still discard. This is a specification model, not GPU/device rendering evidence. `t_unwritten_store` retains real-GPU readback/clear/write/alias cases with corrected store expectations; it is not executed by Windows or software-only CI.
+- **Contract:** [Apple MTLStoreAction.dontCare](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/metal/mtlstoreaction/dontcare) and [load/store actions](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/metal/setting-load-and-store-actions) require preserving contents when they are needed after the pass. Additional stores can increase GPU bandwidth; device frame time and power require acceptance.
+- **History:** the removed optimization was introduced during [NieR:Automata US 1.0.3](../../dm/games/010056B015FE8000/README.md#factory-combat-capture-and-9s-texture-follow-up) performance work. Those measured readbacks did not establish portable preservation semantics. Contract correction found during [Super Mario Odyssey](../../dm/games/0100000000010000/README.md) investigation.
 
 
